# Dev Notes 37 — Runtime Capability Router Contract v1

**Date:** 2026-06-15  
**Branch:** `runtime-capability-router-contract-v1`  
**Repo:** `Main-Michael-Sparks/runtime-dev-repo`  
**Status:** Staged in sandbox; syntax-checked and contract-smoke-tested locally in the assistant sandbox. Not GitHub-verified until Michael uploads/pushes the branch and provides a repo link.

---

## Purpose

Add a contract-only Capability Router metadata and route-plan validation layer under `runtime/bus/`.

This branch answers, in code and tests:

```text
how a normalized Capability Bus action can resolve to a route descriptor
how router metadata validates capability-to-service/backend selection shape
how route definitions remain metadata-only
how route compatibility is checked against the bus-attached capability definition
how route validation rejects missing, disabled, deprecated, duplicate, forbidden, or incompatible routes
how the router contract remains bus-local and non-executing
```

This remains contract-only. It does not make any capability executable.

