## Modular design shape

The `runtime/bus/` namespace remains a contract namespace:

```text
contractValidation.mjs              shared validation result/error helpers and safe object checks
capabilityTaxonomy.mjs              frozen v1 capability/status/event/source-kind constants
capabilityDefinition.mjs            capability definition metadata contract
capabilityRegistryContract.mjs      registry validation, creation, lookup, and listing contract helpers
capabilityBusContract.mjs           non-executing bus intake validation against action + registry contracts
capabilityBusResult.mjs             bus-level skeleton result-envelope constructors
capabilityBusEvents.mjs             bus-level skeleton action-event constructors
capabilityRouterCommon.mjs          shared router constants/copy/prefix/guard helpers
capabilityRouteDefinition.mjs       route metadata definition validation
capabilityRouterRegistry.mjs        router registry validation and lookup helpers
capabilityRoutePlan.mjs             route-plan validation against bus action + registry
capabilityRouterContract.mjs        public barrel for the router contract API
contextRefs.mjs                     context reference validation and normalization
actionEnvelope.mjs                  action request contract validation/normalization
resultEnvelope.mjs                  normalized result/error contract validation/creation
actionEvent.mjs                     action event contract validation/creation
```

The new router contract module imports only existing `runtime/bus/**` contract helpers.

No `runtime.mjs`, `workerBridge.mjs`, `runtime/lifecycle/**`, `runtime/request/**`, `runtime/stream/**`, `runtime/observability/**`, or `llama_worker/**` imports were introduced.

---

## Contract behavior summary

### Capability route definitions

`runtime/bus/capabilityRouterContract.mjs` is a public barrel over split route-definition, registry, and route-plan modules. It exports route-definition helpers:

```text
CAPABILITY_ROUTER_CONTRACT_VERSION
CAPABILITY_ROUTE_STATUSES
isKnownCapabilityRouteStatus()
normalizeCapabilityRouteDefinition()
validateCapabilityRouteDefinition()
assertCapabilityRouteDefinition()
```

Route definitions are metadata only:

```js
const route = {
    routeId: "text-generate-default",
    capability: "text.generate",
    status: "contract-only",
    serviceId: "text.generate.default",
    backendKind: "nativeWorkerBackend",
    backendId: "native-worker.default",
    modelBundleId: "mistral-text-local",
    hardwareProfileId: "laptopFallback",
    requirements: {
        streaming: "supported",
        cancellation: "supported",
        timeout: "supported"
    }
};
```

Validation behavior:

```text
requires routeId, capability, status, serviceId, and backendKind
validates capability names against the v1 capability taxonomy
validates route statuses against the v1 route status list
allows disabled/deprecated route metadata but excludes those routes from route-plan selection
allows backendId/modelBundleId/hardwareProfileId only as metadata IDs
validates optional route requirements using existing support-level semantics
rejects unknown top-level and requirement fields
rejects dangerous/prototype-pollution keys through shared validation helpers
rejects model path/projector path/backend payload/tool process/command/env fields
rejects path-like metadata values
```

### Capability router registry

Registry helpers:

```text
normalizeCapabilityRouterRegistry()
validateCapabilityRouterRegistry()
assertCapabilityRouterRegistry()
createCapabilityRouterRegistry()
listCapabilityRoutes()
getCapabilityRoute()
hasCapabilityRoute()
```

Registry behavior:

```text
schemaVersion defaults to capability-router.v1 when omitted
routes must be an array
nested route definitions are normalized and validated
routeId values must be unique
duplicate selectable routes for the same capability are rejected
disabled/deprecated routes may coexist with one selectable route for the same capability
```

No priority/fallback route ordering was added in this branch.

### Capability route plans

Route-plan helpers:

```text
normalizeCapabilityRoutePlan()
validateCapabilityRoutePlan()
assertCapabilityRoutePlan()
```

Normalized shape:

```js
const routePlan = {
    contractVersion: "capability-router.v1",
    busAction,
    route
};
```

Route-plan validation behavior:

```text
validates busAction as a Capability Bus v1 wrapper
validates nested action envelope and capability definition contracts
validates the router registry
requires the action and capability definition to describe the same capability
selects a route for the requested capability
rejects missing routes
rejects disabled/deprecated-only routes as unselectable
checks route.backendKind against capabilityDefinition.compatibility.backendKinds
requires route.modelBundleId when modelBundleRequired is true
rejects requested streaming when the selected route marks streaming unsupported
rejects contextRefs when capability compatibility disables contextRefs
returns copied/normalized busAction and route descriptors only
```

The route plan is still a descriptor. It does not call a service, call a backend, enqueue a request, emit events, stream tokens, or touch native/model execution.

